  'A Grange hall of 1899, a large gable-roofed clapboard building 30 by 80 feet on a cut stone and rubble foundation. It is now the Fly Creek Area Historical Society\'s museum, in the Fly Creek Historic District, and was listed on the National Register in 2004.',
