  'The Hotel Eagle on this site burned in 1866. Susan Belcher then bought the land and built a house of limestone from the Campbell Quarry, because limestone would not burn. The marker says it keeps its marble fireplaces, glass chandeliers, stencilling and pocket shutters and doors. The Belchers named it Roselawn for its rose gardens.',
